    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on a 2022 f150 with a slipping issue. the diagnostic tool is showing these weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. what are the most likely causes for these kind of pressure fluctuations in the transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes in your 2022 F-150's hydraulic system are most likely caused by a failing transmission torque converter clutch solenoid, which can cycle poorly and cause pressure surges. Other common culprits include worn transmission seals leading to pressure loss, or a stuck shift solenoid creating erratic flow restrictions. Since the slip is causing overheating, it's critical to address these electrical or mechanical faults before they lead to further transmission damage. I recommend having a professional scan for both solenoid codes and check for burnt clutch plates to pinpoint the exact source.",
